From: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dace: launcher consumes the crown (REL_WHEEL wheel + KEY_MENU pushbutton)

The crown wheel (slate-spi, event2) arrives as a QWheelEvent via Qt's generic
evdevmouse plugin, but the launcher's default style
(000-default-horizontal.qml) had no WheelHandler -> the app list did not move.
Also that ListView binds `contentX: tutorialScroll` (a binding to 0), so
contentX must be assigned directly. The crown pushbutton emits KEY_MENU
(139) on event0 (gpio-keys); the AsteroidOS keymap maps it to Qt::Key_MenuKB,
but the home scene does NOT receive keyboard focus (Keys.onPressed never
fired), so it is captured with a GLOBAL event filter
(CrownButtonHandler, same pattern as lipstick's VolumeControl). The crown is
also a high-resolution continuous encoder, so the wheel is damped
(accumulating deltas) both on home and when forwarding to apps
(LipstickCompositorWindow::wheelEvent). All of this is specific to this
variant's hardware (dace / TicWatch Pro 5 with the slate MCU), not upstreamable.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
Signed-off-by: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>

---
diff --git a/lipstick/src/compositor/lipstickcompositorwindow.cpp b/lipstick/src/compositor/lipstickcompositorwindow.cpp
index 7579afb..eb00ed2 100644
--- a/lipstick/src/compositor/lipstickcompositorwindow.cpp
+++ b/lipstick/src/compositor/lipstickcompositorwindow.cpp
@@ -262,7 +262,23 @@ void LipstickCompositorWindow::wheelEvent(QWheelEvent *event)
             inputDevice->sendMouseMoveEvent(v, pos, pos);
         }
         QPoint angle = event->angleDelta();
-        inputDevice->sendMouseWheelEvent(Qt::Vertical, angle.y());
+        // dace/CROWN (2026-09-22): the slate crown is a CONTINUOUS
+        // high-resolution encoder: each REL_WHEEL event is worth 1 and Qt
+        // delivers it as angleDelta.y = 120 (a "notch"). A minimal turn generates
+        // a huge number of events, so they are accumulated and 1 notch is sent
+        // per daceDiv. Increase daceDiv = less sensitive. (This is the APPS path;
+        // home damps it in its QML WheelHandlers.)
+        static int daceWheelAccum = 0;
+        const int daceDiv = 3;
+        daceWheelAccum += angle.y();
+        while (daceWheelAccum >= 120 * daceDiv) {
+            daceWheelAccum -= 120 * daceDiv;
+            inputDevice->sendMouseWheelEvent(Qt::Vertical, 120);
+        }
+        while (daceWheelAccum <= -120 * daceDiv) {
+            daceWheelAccum += 120 * daceDiv;
+            inputDevice->sendMouseWheelEvent(Qt::Vertical, -120);
+        }
     } else {
         event->ignore();
     }
diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 87f77f1..fd4956b 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -5,14 +5,16 @@ set(SRC
 	gesturefilterarea.cpp
 	applauncher.cpp
 	notificationsnoozer.cpp
-	watchfacereloader.cpp)
+	watchfacereloader.cpp
+	crownbuttonhandler.cpp)
 set(HEADERS
 	applauncherbackground.h
 	firstrun.h
 	gesturefilterarea.h
 	applauncher.h
 	notificationsnoozer.h
-	watchfacereloader.h)
+	watchfacereloader.h
